## Conventions & Architectural Rules
- Use WidgetStateProperty (not MaterialStateProperty)
- Use CardThemeData (not CardTheme in ThemeData)
- Feature-based architecture with commons layer
- Keep existing comments and docstrings
- **Interface-First Architecture**: All Services and Repositories MUST have an abstract interface in `lib/interfaces/`
- **Dependency Inversion**: Higher layers (Cubits, Screens, Repos) must depend on Interfaces (e.g. `ILocationService`, `IAuthRepos`), not concrete implementations
- **Unit Test Mocks**: Mock services by `implements IService` to avoid constructor side-effects
- **Equatable Standard**: All BLoC/Cubit states must use `extends Equatable` (NEVER use deprecated `with EquatableMixin` or manual `operator ==`)
- **BLoC/Cubit Purity (Separation of Concerns)**:
  - NEVER hold or manipulate UI Controllers (`MapLibreMapController`, `ScrollController`, `TextEditingController`, `AnimationController`) inside Cubit/BLoC. Cubit is pure state & business logic.
  - UI Widgets hold controllers locally and react to Cubit state changes via `BlocListener` / `BlocConsumer`.
  - NEVER mix UI mixins (`with AppMixin`) or UI Context into Cubits, Services, or Repositories.
  - NEVER use `ValueNotifier` / `ChangeNotifier` controllers alongside Cubits for the same state (No Dual State Management).
  - Use Error Mapping Pattern instead of repetitive duplicate catch blocks in Cubit.
- **UI Architecture & Management Rules**:
  - **No Future in UI (Pure Declarative & Reactive UI)**: UI Widgets are functions of state (`UI = f(State)`). NEVER define `Future<T>` business logic, `async-await`, manual `try-catch`, or ad-hoc `setState(isLoading = true)` inside Widgets. UI triggers synchronous Cubit methods and renders/listens via `BlocConsumer`, `BlocListener`, and `BlocBuilder`.
  - **Controller & Manager Separation**: Complex platform-view or map operations (Marker/Symbol rendering, Sprite asset loading, Camera movement & Bounding Box calculations) MUST be encapsulated in dedicated Manager/Controller classes (e.g. `MapSymbolManager`, `MapCameraController`) in `lib/commons/utils/`. UI Widgets act purely as View wrappers and delegate execution to Managers.
  - **Pure Functions in Helpers**: Computational and transformation algorithms (Haversine distance calculation, sorting by proximity, address/distance formatting, POI unique key extraction, bounding box computation) MUST live in `lib/commons/utils/` (e.g. `PoiCategoryHelper`, `AppUtils`), NOT embedded directly inside Cubits or UI Widgets.
  - **Centralized Route Management**: ALL route paths MUST be declared centrally in `lib/routers/app_routes.dart` (`AppRoutes`). NEVER hardcode string paths (`'/search'`, `'/HomeScreen'`) and NEVER define `static const String path` scattered across individual Screen Widgets. Use `context.go(AppRoutes.home)` or `context.push(AppRoutes.search)`.
- **Localization & i18n Rules**:
  - NEVER hardcode UI strings. All UI text must use `tr(LocaleKeys.xxx)` (wrap in `tr()`).
  - When modifying `assets/translations/vi.json` or `en.json`, ALWAYS run:
    `dart run easy_localization:generate -S assets/translations -O lib/generated; dart run easy_localization:generate -S assets/translations -f keys -O lib/generated -o locale_keys.g.dart`
  - Avoid duplicate keys between primitive Strings and nested Maps (e.g. use separate `notification_tabs` namespace if `notification` is a string).
